Subject: [PATCH] sparse: bound the raw chunk bounce buffer

write_sparse_chunk_raw() allocates FASTBOOT_MAX_BLK_WRITE storage blocks
for its aligned copy. On NAND the block is a page, so with 16 KiB pages
that is 256 MiB, more than the malloc pool; the allocation fails and the
whole sparse write is aborted with only a fastboot reply. Size the
buffer like the fill buffer, from CONFIG_IMAGE_SPARSE_FILLBUF_SIZE.

---
 lib/image-sparse.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/lib/image-sparse.c b/lib/image-sparse.c
index 09225692e9b..1a7c5bf6d8c 100644
--- a/lib/image-sparse.c
+++ b/lib/image-sparse.c
@@ -55,7 +55,9 @@ static lbaint_t write_sparse_chunk_raw(struct sparse_storage *info,
 				       char *response)
 {
 	lbaint_t n = blkcnt, write_blks, blks = 0;
-	lbaint_t aligned_buf_blks = FASTBOOT_MAX_BLK_WRITE;
+	lbaint_t aligned_buf_blks = clamp_t(lbaint_t,
+					    CONFIG_IMAGE_SPARSE_FILLBUF_SIZE / info->blksz,
+					    1, FASTBOOT_MAX_BLK_WRITE);
 	uint32_t *aligned_buf = NULL;
 
 	if (CONFIG_IS_ENABLED(SYS_DCACHE_OFF)) {
